      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report the case of a 41-year-old man with acute myocardial infarction showing first ST elevation in V1-V6-DI-aVL leads followed by a typical V2-V4 ST depression (concomitant occlusion of proximal diagonal branch with an incomplete left anterior descending occlusion) and DII-DIII-aVF ST elevation. At coronary angiography, a proximal left anterior descending coronary stenosis with right coronary artery thrombosis was found."},
